[0.45, "o", "Title:      \u001b[1mShip Installable Linux And Mac Developer Experience\u001b[0m\r\nStatus:     \u001b[1m\u001b[92mverified\u001b[39m\u001b[0m\r\nArchetype:  \u001b[95m\u001b[1mStrategic\u001b[0m\u001b[39m\r\n\u001b[2m\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1mGoals\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mMG-01\u001b[0m - Convert bearing VDcT0vaPb into executable board work for an installable Linux and macOS developer experience. (\u001b[2mVDcT0vaPb\u001b[0m)\r\n  \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mMG-02\u001b[0m - Keep the mission surfaces doctor-clean and make this installable developer-experience mission visible through the board command surfaces. (\u001b[2mrun `just keel mission show VDcdHpbFp`, `just flow`, and `just keel doctor`\u001b[0m)\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mChildren\u001b[0m\r\n  Epics (1):\r\n    \u001b[1m\u001b[36mVDcT0vaPb\u001b[39m\u001b[0m - Installable Linux And Mac Developer Experience (\u001b[2mdone\u001b[0m)\r\n  Bearings (1):\r\n    \u001b[1m\u001b[94mVDcT0vaPb\u001b[39m\u001b[0m - Installable Linux And Mac Developer Experience (\u001b[2mlaid\u001b[0m)\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mStructural Drift\u001b[0m\r\n  Coefficient: 0.63 (severe)\r\n  Coverage:    entities 302/302 | knowledge 5/43 | source 0/0 | docs 0/17\r\n  Context:     38 knowledge units lack source provenance; 17 project docs are unlinked\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mLatest Log Entry\u001b[0m\r\n    2026-03-11T21:00:18\r\n"]
[1.8, "o", "$ sed -n '1,120p' .keel/missions/VDcdHpbFp/CHARTER.md\r\n"]
[2.25, "o", "# Ship Installable Linux And Mac Developer Experience - Charter\r\n\r\n## Goals\r\n\r\n| ID | Description | Verification |\r\n|----|-------------|--------------|\r\n| MG-01 | Convert bearing VDcT0vaPb into executable board work for an installable Linux and macOS developer experience. | board: VDcT0vaPb |\r\n| MG-02 | Keep the mission surfaces doctor-clean and make this installable developer-experience mission visible through the board command surfaces. | manual: run `just keel mission show VDcdHpbFp`, `just flow`, and `just keel doctor` |\r\n\r\n## Constraints\r\n- Keep one canonical `port` CLI and guest model across Linux and macOS, use VDcT0vaPb plus `RELEASE.md`, `README.md`, and `docs/avf.md` as the primary sources, and avoid broadening scope into new runtime substrates or separate platform-specific toolchains.\r\n- Preserve the hard-cutover policy: do not add compatibility aliases or dual-surface operator paths just to ease packaging.\r\n\r\n## Halting Rules\r\n\r\n- DO NOT halt while any MG-* goal has unfinished board work\r\n- HALT when the installable developer-experience work is decomposed into executable board items and only verification-oriented manual checks remain\r\n- YIELD to human when prioritization depends on external signing, packaging-channel, or distribution decisions that are not inferable from the repository\r\n"]
[3.6, "o", "$ keel epic show VDcT0vaPb\r\n"]
[4.05, "o", "Title:     \u001b[1mInstallable Linux And Mac Developer Experience\u001b[0m\r\nStatus:    \u001b[32mdone\u001b[39m\r\nCreated:   \u001b[2m2026-03-11 21:12:35\u001b[0m\r\nStarted:   \u001b[2m2026-03-11 21:19:16\u001b[0m\r\nUpdated:   \u001b[2m2026-03-11 22:11:31\u001b[0m\r\nCompleted: \u001b[2m2026-03-11 22:11:31\u001b[0m (\u001b[2m52m\u001b[0m)\r\nPath:      \u001b[2m/home/alex/workspace/spoke-sh/port/.keel/epics/VDcT0vaPb/README.md\u001b[0m\r\nPRD:       \u001b[2m/home/alex/workspace/spoke-sh/port/.keel/epics/VDcT0vaPb/PRD.md\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1mProblem\u001b[0m\r\n  Port already ships real Linux and macOS lanes, but the release contract is\r\n  still repo-centric:\r\n  ...\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mGoals\u001b[0m\r\n  - \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-01\u001b[0m: Publish a concrete Linux and macOS support matrix. (\u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mREADME.md\u001b[0m and \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mRELEASE.md\u001b[0m define the supported targets and operator boundary for the first installable slice. -> First voyage complete)\r\n  - \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-02\u001b[0m: Ship one canonical package contract for the \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mport\u001b[0m CLI. (Repo-local workflows can produce a stable install artifact per supported target with explicit included files and install steps. -> First voyage complete)\r\n  - \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-03\u001b[0m: Make the macOS AVF distribution boundary explicit. (Docs and doctor/help surfaces explain the AVF launcher-helper requirement and entitlement boundary for distributed macOS targets. -> First voyage complete)\r\n  - \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-04\u001b[0m: Keep release validation anchored on canonical Port workflows. (The first release proof uses \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mjust\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mport doctor\u001b[0m, workspace tests, and board checks instead of ad hoc packaging-only scripts. -> First voyage complete)\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mScope Drift\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2m(no scope drift detected)\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mStructural Drift\u001b[0m\r\n  Coefficient: 0.63 (severe)\r\n  Coverage:    entities 302/302 | knowledge 5/43 | source 0/0 | docs 0/17\r\n  Context:     38 knowledge units lack source provenance; 17 project docs are unlinked\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mRequirement Coverage\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36mFR-01\u001b[39m - Port must publish a concrete support matrix for the first installable Linux and macOS targets, including explicit operator boundaries for unsupported environments.\r\n    Linked goals (2): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-01\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-04\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVDchK6xzs\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-01\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mFR-02\u001b[39m - Port must define one canonical package artifact format and output layout for the supported targets so operators can install the \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mport\u001b[0m CLI without starting from a repo checkout.\r\n    Linked goals (2): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-01\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-02\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVDchK6xzs\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-03\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mFR-03\u001b[39m - The repository must provide a repo-local packaging workflow that builds the supported install artifacts and documents the install steps and included files.\r\n    Linked goals (2): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-02\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-04\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVDchK6xzs\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-02\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mFR-04\u001b[39m - Port must make the macOS AVF launcher-helper and entitlement boundary explicit in the install and release contract without introducing a second macOS-only operator model.\r\n    Linked goals (2): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-03\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-04\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVDchK6xzs\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-04\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mFR-05\u001b[39m - Release validation for the installable slice must remain anchored on canonical \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mjust\u001b[0m and \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mport\u001b[0m commands, including board health and doctor checks.\r\n    Linked goals (2): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-02\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-04\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVDchK6xzs\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-05\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mNFR-01\u001b[39m - Package naming, included files, and install instructions must be deterministic for each supported target.\r\n    Linked goals (2): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-01\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-02\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (2): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVDchK6xzs\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-NFR-01\u001b[39m, \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVDchK6xzs\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-NFR-03\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mNFR-02\u001b[39m - Unsupported targets or incomplete packaging prerequisites must fail fast with explicit guidance rather than silently falling back to a source-only workflow.\r\n    Linked goals (3): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-01\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-02\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-03\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVDchK6xzs\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-NFR-02\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mNFR-03\u001b[39m - The first voyage must end with executable implementation stories and concrete verification commands, not another packaging roadmap placeholder.\r\n    Linked goals (4): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-01\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-02\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-03\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-04\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVDchK6xzs\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-NFR-04\u001b[39m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mPress Release\u001b[0m\r\n  Status:     \u001b[2mnot authored\u001b[0m\r\n  Guidance:   optional; use for large user-facing value shifts\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mProgress\u001b[0m\r\n  Voyages:              1/1 \u001b[32m\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u001b[39m \u001b[32m1/1\u001b[39m\r\n  Stories:              4/4 \u001b[32m\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u001b[39m \u001b[32m4/4\u001b[39m\r\n  ETA:                  complete\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mVerification Strategy\u001b[0m\r\n  Techniques:\r\n    - Area: Method\r\n    - macOS AVF boundary: automated test + inspection\r\n    - packaging workflow: command proof + automated test\r\n    - release validation path: command proof\r\n    - support matrix and release contract: inspection + command proof\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mVerification Readiness\u001b[0m\r\n  Criteria:              automated 18 | manual 0\r\n  Requirement coverage:  automated 8 | manual 0\r\n  Artifact inventory:    text 9 | media 0 | other 0\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mVoyages\u001b[0m\r\n  \u00